# Project Structure

.
├── agents/ - Intensive learning agents
            Naming convention: the agent used for each experimental scenario is named experiment_ppo/gradient_agnet.py (for example:2players_ppo_agent.py)
├── envs/ - game environment
├── config/ - Experiment configuration
            one_stage_two_players [one_stage_two_players.py](mdc:config/one_stage_two_players.py)
            one_stage_three_players [one_stage_three_players.py](mdc:config/one_stage_three_players.py)
            two_stage_two_players [two_stage_two_players.py](mdc:config/two_stage_two_players.py)
            asymmetric_cost_two_players [asymmetric_cost_two_players.py](mdc:config/asymmetric_cost_two_players.py)
            asymmetric_ability_two_players [asymmetric_ability_two_players.py](mdc:config/asymmetric_ability_two_players.py)
├── run/ - Experiment execution scripts
            No matter how many files are generated in the middle of the experiment (e.g., test, comparison, etc.), the final code is uniformly summarized in the
            [run_asymmetric_ability_experiment.py](mdc:run/run_asymmetric_ability_experiment.py)
            [run_asymmetric_cost_experiment.py](mdc:run/run_asymmetric_cost_experiment.py)
            [run_three_players.py](mdc:run/run_three_players.py)
            [run_two_players.py](mdc:run/run_two_players.py)
            [run_two_stage.py](mdc:run/run_two_stage.py)
├── results/ - experiment results
            All chart headers are
            stage1_weight,stage2_weight,k1,k2,information_revelation,theoretical_stage1_effort,theoretical_stage2_effort,Model_training,final_stage1_effort,final_stage2_effort,final_weighted_effort,Convergence_Quality,episodes,Gap_from_theoretical
            The chart name is the same as its config
            all run.py scripts produce results that match the results table header
└── utils/ - utility functions
